// S14 — Map<K,V>::get leaves the value type unresolved through an if-let binding.
//
// Expected: no errors. `strings` is fully annotated !Map<String, u32>, so
// `get` should yield Option<u32> and `?id` should bind a u32.
//
// Actual:  [E0003] type mismatch in return: expected U32!, found Option<?1..>
//
// Contrast: the identical shape over a plain Option field checks clean, so the
// gap is specifically in resolving a generic Map's value type, not in if-let.

☉ Σ I { strings: !Map<String, u32> }

⊢ I {
    ☉ rite intern(Δ self, s: !&str) -> !u32 {
        ⎇ ≔ ?id = self.strings.get(s) {
            ⤺ id;
        }
        ↩ 0;
    }
}
